pseudo-Boolean proof version 2.0
* The version 2.0 spelling. `red` with an EMPTY witness is treated as a proof by contradiction
* (red_strengthening.rs), and an empty witness touches no database constraint, so
* `database.get_proofgoals()` registers none either -- `proofgoal 1` lands in the same
* fabrication branch. Same forged UNSAT for the same satisfiable clause.
f 1
red >= 1 ; ; begin
    proofgoal 1
        u >= 1 ;
    end
end
output NONE
conclusion UNSAT
end pseudo-Boolean proof
